# =============================================================================
# .dockerignore — RouterFuel
#
# Without this file Docker ships the whole working directory to the daemon as
# build context on every single build — ./target alone is ~2.5 GB, plus
# ./models and a real .env. The Dockerfile only ever COPYs Cargo.toml,
# Cargo.lock, src/, migrations/ and static/, so everything else is dead weight
# that buys nothing but a slower build.
#
# .env stays excluded even though this Dockerfile never COPYs it: the published
# image is public, and a future `COPY . .` would otherwise bake local secrets
# straight into it. Cheap insurance.
# =============================================================================

# Rust build output — by far the biggest offender.
target/

# Optional ONNX embedding model + tokenizer. Mounted at runtime as a volume
# (see docker-compose.yml), never needed at build time.
models/

# Local secrets.
.env
.env.*

# Version control, editor and agent scratch files.
.git/
.gitignore
.aider*
.vscode/
.idea/

# Docs and container config — not inputs to the compiled binary.
*.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
